@startuml SABER Benchmark Framework Architecture - Actual Implementation

!theme plain
title SABER Benchmark Framework - Task Definition Management (Client-Side Orchestration)

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor black
    ArrowColor black
    FontSize 10
}

package "Benchmark Framework Core" {

    class BenchmarkManager {
        +domain: str
        +config_dir: Path
        +tasks_file_path: Path
        +tasks: Dict[str, Task]
        +benchmark_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +config_loader: BenchmarkConfigLoader
        --
        +load_tasks_from_yaml(): void
        +get_benchmark_info(): BenchmarkInfo
        +get_task(task_id: str): Task
        +get_subtask(task_id: str, subtask_id: str): SubTask
        +list_tasks(): List[Dict[str, Any]]
        +get_benchmark_config(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_episode_config(task_id: str): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_permanent_environment(): Optional[str]
    }

    class BenchmarkSession {
        +session_id: str
        +benchmark_info: BenchmarkInfo
        +config: Dict[str, Any]
        --
        +to_api_response(domain: str): Dict[str, Any]
        +domain: str (property)
        +total_tasks: int (property)
        +total_episodes: int (property)
    }

    class BenchmarkInfo {
        +domain: str
        +tasks: List[TaskInfo]
        +total_tasks: int
        +total_episodes: int
        --
        +to_dict(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_task_by_id(task_id: str): TaskInfo?
        +get_task_ids(): List[str]
    }

    class TaskInfo {
        +task_id: str
        +title: str
        +description: str
        +episode_attempts: int
        +subtask_count: int
    }

    class BenchmarkConfigLoader {
        +domain: str
        +allowed_executors: Optional[List[str]]
        +benchmark_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +global_defaults: Dict[str, Any]
        +permanent_environment: Optional[str]
        +yaml_data: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
        --
        +load_tasks_from_file(tasks_file_path: str): Dict[str, Task]
        +load_benchmark_config(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_permanent_environment(task_id: str): Optional[str]
        +get_allowed_executors(): List[str]
        +_parse_task(task_data: Dict): Task
        +_parse_subtask(subtask_data: Dict): SubTask
        +_parse_benchmark_config(yaml_data: Dict): Dict[str, Any]
        +_parse_permanent_environment(yaml_data: Dict): Optional[str]
    }

    class Task {
        +task_id: str
        +domain: str
        +title: str
        +description: str
        +subtasks: List[SubTask]
        +initial_context: Dict[str, Any]
        +environment: Union[str, Dict[str, Any]]
        +allowed_executors: Optional[List[str]]
        +execution_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +episode_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +benchmark_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +_subtask_map: Dict[str, SubTask]
        --
        +add_subtask(subtask: SubTask): void
        +get_subtask_by_id(subtask_id: str): Optional[SubTask]
        +is_complete(): bool
        +get_all_subtask_ids(): Set[str]
        +get_episode_attempts(): int
        +get_environment_config(): Dict[str, Any]
    }

    class SubTask {
        +subtask_id: str
        +task_id: str
        +title: str
        +description: str
        +objective: str
        +dependencies: Optional[List[str]]
        --
        +is_dependent_on(subtask_id: str): bool
    }
}

package "Episode Management (Pydantic Models in base.py)" {

    class EpisodeManager {
        +active_episodes: Dict[str, Episode]
        +episode_configs: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]
        --
        +configure_for_task(session_id: str, task: Task): void
        +should_terminate_episode(session_id: str): tuple[bool, str]
        +start_episode(session_id: str, task_id: str, initial_context?: Dict): Episode
        +step(session_id: str, action: Action, command_result: CommandResult): StepResult
        +end_episode(session_id: str, reason: str): Episode
        +reset_episode(session_id: str, task_id: str): Episode
        +get_episode_state(session_id: str): Optional[EpisodeState]
        +get_current_episode(session_id: str): Optional[Episode]
        +create_step(episode: Episode, action: Action, response: Dict): Step
        +update_episode_state(episode: Episode, step: Step): void
        +cleanup_session(session_id: str): void
    }

    class Episode {
        +episode_id: str
        +task_id: str
        +session_id: str
        +start_time: datetime
        +end_time: Optional[datetime]
        +state: EpisodeState
        +steps: List[Step]
        +context: Dict[str, Any]
        +metadata: Dict[str, Any]
        +completion_reason: Optional[str]
        --
        +add_step(step: Step): void
        +get_executed_commands(): List[str]
        +is_complete: bool (property)
        +duration: Optional[float] (property)
    }

    class Step {
        +step_number: int
        +timestamp: datetime
        +action: Action
        +response: Dict[str, Any]
        +context_snapshot: Dict[str, Any]
        +done: bool
    }

    class Action {
        +tool_name: str
        +parameters: Dict[str, Any]
        +timestamp: datetime
    }

    class StepResult {
        +step: Step
        +should_terminate: bool
        +termination_reason: Optional[str]
    }

    enum EpisodeState {
        CREATED
        ACTIVE
        COMPLETED
        FAILED
        TIMEOUT
        RESET
    }
}

' Relationships
BenchmarkManager *-- BenchmarkConfigLoader
BenchmarkManager *-- Task
BenchmarkManager ..> BenchmarkInfo : creates
BenchmarkManager ..> BenchmarkSession : creates

BenchmarkConfigLoader ..> Task : creates
BenchmarkConfigLoader ..> SubTask : creates

BenchmarkSession *-- BenchmarkInfo
BenchmarkInfo *-- TaskInfo

Task *-- SubTask

EpisodeManager *-- Episode
Episode *-- Step
Step *-- Action
Episode ..> EpisodeState
EpisodeManager ..> StepResult : returns

note top of BenchmarkManager
**Task Definition Manager (Not Orchestrator)**
Simplified to focus on YAML parsing and task lookup.
No longer handles server-side benchmark sessions or task queues.
Client-side orchestration responsibility moved to harness implementations.
Provides BenchmarkInfo for client-side task management.
Supports permanent environment configuration for network connectivity.
Enhanced Task objects contain complete execution and episode configuration.
end note

note top of BenchmarkSession
**Simple Session Wrapper**
Lightweight wrapper around BenchmarkInfo with optional config.
No task queue management or progression logic.
Pure data container for API responses.
Task orchestration moved to client responsibility.
end note

note top of Task
**Complete Task Configuration Container**
Enhanced with flexible environment specification:
- String: Template reference (e.g., "dvwa_pentest")
- Dict: Full environment config or hybrid approach
Includes execution_config, episode_config, and benchmark_config.
No longer uses "sandbox_environment" field name.
Contains all parameters needed by ExecutionManager and EpisodeManager.
Supports permanent environment integration for network tasks.
end note

note top of EpisodeManager
**RL Episode Lifecycle Manager**
Configured per task with episode_config validation.
Returns StepResult tuples with termination information.
Manages episode state transitions and step tracking.
Single source of truth for episode operations.
Task-specific configuration (max_steps, timeouts) required.
end note

note top of BenchmarkConfigLoader
**Enhanced YAML Parser with Permanent Environment Support**
Parses complete task configuration including:
- Environment specifications (flexible format)
- Execution configuration (timeouts, limits)
- Episode configuration (max_steps, timeouts)
- Benchmark configuration (episode_attempts)
- Permanent environment settings for network connectivity
Validates domain consistency and required fields.
Single responsibility: YAML → Task object conversion.
end note

note bottom of Episode
**Pydantic Model in base.py**
All episode-related models are Pydantic BaseModel classes.
Provides JSON serialization and validation.
Complete action-response history for RL training.
Properties for computed values (duration, is_complete).
No subtask progression tracking - pure episode data.
end note

@enduml
